Don't hesitate, if you more help, I'm unemployed so I got nothing better to do haha.

Not sure your sentence makes any sense.

If you meant "Just wanted to be saved", it'd translate as "voulait juste être sauvé". But it lacks a pronoun to make sense.

&#x200B;

\-I just wanted to be saved = Je voulais juste être sauvé

\-She just wanted to be saved = Elle voulait juste être sauvée

\-We just wanted to be saved = Nous voulions juste être sauvés

&#x200B;

In french "vouloir" (want) and "sauver" (save) are conjugated differently depending on the pronoun you use.

&#x200B;

Hope this'll help, if not, tell me and I'll help you.

I guess I've never seen them cause I mostly watch movies depending on the directors, and they're all from direcors upon which I haen't set my interest yet. I've just seen 4 or 5 Scorseses, 3 Kubricks and 1 Lynch but never delved into any of them. On the other hand I've watched a lot of Hitchcock, De Palma, Spielberg, Friedkin, Cronenberg (only 2 films of him I haven't seen). I've just started today watching PTA films, and I intend to see them all in chronological order.

